                <zone fixed-size='1117' forceUpdate='true' h='9300' id='377' type-v2='text' w='73831' x='3277' y='9500'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='11'>This Tableau project was built using </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#ee1c4d' fontsize='11'>Python</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='11'> to generate fake customer email data and display both my Python and Tableau abilities. A summary of things done is outlined below and a more </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ee1c4d' fontsize='11'>detailed descriptio</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#ee1c4d' fontsize='11'>n</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='11'> together with Python scripts can be found on my </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ee1c4d' fontsize='11'>GitHub</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='11'> page (click the button on the right). </run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone alt-text='Click to view on GitHub' fixed-size='69' h='9300' id='376' is-fixed='true' is-scaled='1' param='Image/Group 1 (1).png' type-v2='bitmap' url='https://github.com/Marius321/Email-Marketing-Campaign-Dashboard' w='19615' x='77108' y='9500'>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='356' forceUpdate='true' h='35100' id='367' type-v2='text' w='24416' x='44641' y='19900'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='14'>2. Writing code</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>There are three Python scripts used to generate the datasets for this project:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>1. Email Data Generating Script - generates</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ee1c4d' fontsize='11'>fake data</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>and email metrics</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>2. Filtering Script -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ee1c4d' fontsize='11'>filters</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>the output from the previous script based on certain percentiles</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>3. Sankey Script - transforms data into a suitable format for building a</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ee1c4d' fontsize='11'>Sankey Funnel Chart</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                    <format attr='background-color' value='#1b242cb4' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='35100' id='399' type-v2='text' w='28380' x='69057' y='19900'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='14'>3. Tableau Functionality</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>- Parameter and select actions</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>- Navigation buttons</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>- Gradient images created using Figma</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>- Custom number formatting to display up/down indicators</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>- Sankey funnel chart following this blog:</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run auto-url='true' fontsize='11' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://www.flerlagetwins.com/2019/11/sankey-funnel.html&amp;quot;'>https://www.flerlagetwins.com/2019/11/sankey-funnel.html</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#e5e5e5' fontsize='11'>- Gradient bar chart:</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run auto-url='true' fontsize='11' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NwV6FWAbPAM&amp;quot;'>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NwV6FWAbPAM</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
